# Example Caddy config for prodbox. Caddy is the only thing facing the
# internet (SPEC.md #12): every container port is bound to 127.0.0.1, and
# Caddy runs on the host (not inside docker/compose.yml), terminating TLS and
# reverse-proxying to the loopback port this stack's web service published.
#
# Copy to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile, replace the domain, reload Caddy.
#
# Two isolated stacks live on this box, prod and preview (SPEC.md #12), each
# with its own subdomain and its own web container on a different loopback
# port. Both DNS records must be grey-clouded (Cloudflare: DNS-only, proxy
# switch off) rather than orange-clouded, or Caddy cannot complete its own
# ACME challenge and terminate TLS directly:
#
#   canonry.example.com          A/AAAA  <prodbox IP>   ; prod, grey-clouded
#   preview.canonry.example.com  A/AAAA  <prodbox IP>   ; preview, grey-clouded

canonry.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5196
}

# Preview stack: same shape, its own compose project and its own web port.
# preview.canonry.example.com {
# 	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5296
# }
